// A word's or symbol's FEATURES from the feature cache, for pgGet.
// The far route (psGet) searches the property lists, then the lexicon's entry
// (for a symbol a scan of gTwins) before it finds the cache's slot.
// This hashes the atom to its slot as psSlot does and takes the list if it is made.
// The cache's keys are made only by psLex, after the atom's property list
// had no FEATURES. A made list is the answer unless FEATURES has been
// put on an atom since. psPut then sets psHotOff, and this finds nothing
// until the sentence's end clears both (psClear).
// A key of the negative kinds is a ROOT's (psLex complements the kind bits),
// never an atom's.
// Bank 5, eem on. Needs shrdlu.ah (PFC, PFCN), pgm.ac's pgGx and pgsys.ac's
// psHotOff.

// Takes the atom in pgGx.
// Returns to the word after the call with IO = the list, if the atom's list is
// made. Returns to the call's return address otherwise.
// AC and IO are clobbered.
// Called via jsp from bank 6, with the return address in AC.
psHot,
    local loop, found, miss, ret, p
    dac ret
    lac i [psHotOff:012]
    sza
    jmp miss
    lac i [pgGx:6]
    spa
    jmp miss
    and [PFCN-1]
    ral 1s
    ior [PFC]
    dac p
    // A slot is a key, then its list; an empty slot's key and list are 0.
loop, lac i p
#ifndef HOTANY
    sad i [pgGx:6]
    jmp found
    sza i
    jmp found
#else
    jmp found               // HOTANY: take the first slot, whatever its key
#endif
    law 2
    add p
    and [0777777-(PFCN<<1)]     // the table's end wraps to its start
    dac p
    jmp loop
found, idx p
    lio i p
    spi
    idx ret
miss, jmp i ret
ret, 0
p, 0
    endloc
